   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERT OF INS.   REF PH-45367\nNorthern Shield Assurance   POL NO EL-920074\nINSURED ....... Westbrook Youth League\nRISK LOCATION .. Old Quay\nFROM .......... 2027-10-22\nTO ............ 2027-10-24\nINDEMNITY ..... $2,000,000\nACTIVITY ...... Foot race (Westbrook Open Race 5K)\nISSUED ........ 2027-05-28\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Westbrook Open Race 5K - medical notes\nSaturday 23 October 2027 / gun 08:00 / 160 runners / 5K\ncontact Priya Raman 555-0198\nWe expect a crew from Sentinel Ambulance Service on the day, though we have nothing in writing yet.\n\nFIRST AID\n3 posts (start, finish, midpoint). 8 qualified first aiders. nowhere more than 1.5km from a post. 2 bike responders w/ defibs\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\nNorthshore District Hospital, 16km from finish. pickup point the top of Weir Street, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nFatima Haddad, registered paramedic, on site from -1hr til last runner in. can withdraw any runner\n\npast yrs: last runner well inside limit, only blisters + one twisted ankle. some members have work first aid certs, general helping\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nWestbrook Open Race 5K | Saturday 23 October 2027\nOrganiser: Westbrook Youth League\nRace director: Priya Raman\nReference: RQ-83277\n\nOverview\nThe Westbrook Open Race 5K is a 5K race of 5 km for 160 entrants, based in the Old Quay area of Port Halden. The start is at 08:00 and the course closes at 09:15.\n\nCourse\nThe course runs in order along Weir Street, Cooper Street, Foundry Street and Copper Row, all of which are closed to traffic for the race. Major roads crossed: Canal Road, Regent Road, Tram Street, Queen's Road, Dock Road and Victoria Road. The finish is in Market Square.\n\nCourse dimensions\nMost of the course follows the older street grid. Measured building line to building line, Weir Street is about 4 m, Copper Row about 4 m, and parked vehicles on Foundry Street leave around 5 m. The field assembles on Weir Street over that width, and the finish chute is laid out in the same street, ahead of Market Square.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the top of Weir Street from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Westbrook website the same day.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "traffic_plan.txt",
    "text": "TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT PLAN\nEvent: Westbrook Open Race 5K\nDate: Saturday 23 October 2027\nApplicant: Westbrook Youth League\nPrepared by: Brightway Traffic Consulting\nIssue: 1.2\n\n1. Scope\nThis plan describes how traffic will be managed for the Westbrook Open Race 5K, a 5K race in the Old Quay area of Port Halden with a 08:00 start. It has been prepared to accompany the permit application and should be read with the race plan. We have not arranged any police attendance for this race.\n\n2. Road closures\nTemporary closures will be in force as follows, with barriers and advance signing supplied by Pathfinder Road Crews.\n- Weir Street, Quay Street to Canon Road: closed 06:45 to 09:45\n- Cooper Street, Canon Road to Glebe Road: closed 06:45 to 09:45\n- Foundry Street, Union Row to Canon Road: closed 06:45 to 09:45\n- Copper Row, Dyer Street to Union Row: closed 06:45 to 09:45\n\n3. Major crossings\nEach major crossing has its own control point, staffed from 06:45 until the last runner has passed.\n- Canal Road at Weir Street: 3 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Regent Road at Cooper Street: 2 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Tram Street at Copper Row: 4 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Queen's Road at Weir Street: 2 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Dock Road at Copper Row: 3 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Victoria Road at Foundry Street: 2 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n\n4. Diversions\nSigned diversions will operate for the duration of the closures.\n- Weir Street: traffic diverted via Cross Avenue and Prince Street, signed from Canon Road\n- Cooper Street: traffic diverted via Church Road and Ferry Road, signed from Dyer Street\n- Foundry Street: traffic diverted via Prince Street and Ferry Road, signed from Canon Road\n- Copper Row: traffic diverted via High Street and Church Road, signed from Dyer Street\n\n5. Emergency vehicle access\nA clear lane of at least 3.5 m will be kept along the closed section for emergency vehicles. Barrier staff hold radios on the event channel and can open any closure within two minutes on request from the event controller, who is in direct contact with the police and ambulance control rooms.\n\n6. Notification\nAll frontages on the closed streets receive a letter drop 21 days before the event, with a further reminder at 7 days. Advance notice signs go up 10 days before, and bus operators have been given the closure times.\n\n7. Reopening\nA sweep vehicle follows the last runner. Closures are lifted in the order listed, after a barrier and litter check, with all roads open by 09:45.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nPlease find our application below.\n\nHere is our application for the Westbrook Open Race 5K, Saturday 23 October 2027. 160 runners, 5K, off at 08:00, around Old Quay. I've attached insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt, traffic_plan.txt. We have also lined up Sentinel Ambulance Service for the day.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThanks,\nPriya\n\nPriya Raman, Westbrook Youth League\n555-0198\n",
